      "authority": "PAULA_DIRECT_2026_11_10",
      "rule": "For an insurer statement listing pending requirements, capture EVERY contractual requirement (overdue, currently due and future) as a separate uniquely identified receivable in the exact policy edition. Classify based on actual per-requirement due date versus an explicit statement cutoff; at processing time distinguish an older as-of snapshot from today. Due date before the comparison date and still outstanding = vencido; currently due within insurer billing window = cuota vigente; later due = cobro futuro. A pending statement is NOT itself evidence of payment. Explicit paid-collection statements are a different source category."
